                    <table align="center" role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
                      <tr>
                        <td class="h1 pb20">Can an oHCM treatment help patients avoid surgery?</td>
                      </tr>
                      <!-- end h1 header -->
                      <tr>
                        <td class="p pb20 m-pb15">For people living with obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy (oHCM), symptoms and obstruction can impact the ability to be active day to day. When the effect is significant, your doctor may suggest septal reduction therapies (SRTs).</td>
                      </tr>
                      <!-- end paragraph -->
                      <tr>
                        <td class="pink bold">What are SRTs?</td>
                      </tr>
                      <!-- end paragraph -->
                      <tr>
                        <td class="pb20">SRTs are procedures that improve blood flow by thinning the heart wall via surgery or by alcohol septal ablation. A clinical study looked at the number of days people taking MYQORZOTM were eligible for SRTs.*</td>
                      </tr>
                      <!-- end paragraph -->
                    </table>
                    <!-- end table block -->
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="footnote pb20 m-pb30">
                    <table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                      <tr>
                        <td class="li" valign="top">*</td>
                        <td>MYQORZO was studied in a 24-week, Phase 3, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical trial of 282 people with symptomatic obstructive HCM to see the impact on peak oxygen consumption (peak VO<sub>2</sub>) and duration of eligibility for SRT. Eligibility criteria include severe symptoms (New York Heart Association class III or IV) and severe obstruction (left ventricular outflow gradient ≥50 mmHg).</td>
                      </tr>
                    </table>
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <!-- end footnote list -->
